# upstream tarballs — re-downloadable from sourceforge.net/projects/sigel
*.tar.gz

# The two the build needs are tracked, in vendor/, so a clone builds with no
# download: vendor/pvm3.4.6.tgz (its extension keeps it out of the rule above)
# and vendor/supportingLibs.tar.gz (the exception below). netlib is PVM's last
# host -- Fedora retired it in 2015, Debian removed it in 2024, and the only
# other copies are Debian's pvm_3.4.6.orig.tar.gz and an AUR PKGBUILD -- and
# sourceforge is the only other copy of the supporting libraries. Everything
# else that matches the rule stays untracked, so a new archive here needs
# `git add -f' or its own exception.
!vendor/supportingLibs.tar.gz

# extracted 2003 i386 binary; the tarball and the tree are both gone, and this
# keeps a re-extract out of `git status'
xb/

# vendored deps (Qt 2.3, dynamechs, SOLID, cv97, newmat09, qhull, fparser,
# Dynamo) — separate upstream tarball, out of scope for the Qt port.
# Extracted from vendor/supportingLibs.tar.gz. pvm3/ lives here too but comes
# from vendor/pvm3.4.6.tgz, not from that tarball.
x/supportingLibs/

# older 1.0 release, not used
x/sigelSourceDistribution.1.0/

build/

build-fast/

# python bytecode
__pycache__/

# Written next to Terrain.ter while it is being generated; a killed process
# leaves one behind.
Terrain.ter.*
